@{
    ViewData["Title"] = T("Community Standards") + " — DashLane";
    Layout = "_AuthLayout";
}

<div class="legal-page has-toc">
    <aside class="legal-toc" data-toc aria-label="@T("On this page")"><p>@T("On this page")</p><ol></ol></aside>

    <article class="legal-card">
        <p class="legal-kicker">DashLane Mobility</p>
        <h1 class="legal-title">@T("Community Standards")</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">@T("Last updated: November 10, 2026")</p>
        @if (IsFrench)
        {
            <p class="notice legal-lang-note">@T("This document is currently available in English only.")</p>
        }

        <p class="legal-lead">
            DashLane works because strangers trust each other enough to share a car for a few hours. These standards describe what every member can expect
            from everyone else, and what we'll do when someone falls short. They apply to every member, on and off the road, from the moment you create an account.
        </p>

        <div class="legal-summary">
            <h2>The short version</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><span><strong>Be real.</strong> Your account, photo and ID must be yours and accurate.</span></li>
                <li><span><strong>Be safe.</strong> Drive legally and soberly, and never pressure anyone into an unsafe situation.</span></li>
                <li><span><strong>Be respectful.</strong> No harassment, discrimination or unwanted contact — ever.</span></li>
                <li><span><strong>Be reliable.</strong> Show up when you said you would, and say so early if plans change.</span></li>
            </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-callout is-danger">
            @Icon.Get("alert", 18)
            <span><strong>If you or anyone else is in immediate danger, call 911 first.</strong> DashLane can't dispatch emergency services. Report the incident to us once you're safe.</span>
        </div>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>1. Identity and honesty</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Use your real legal name and date of birth, and a recent photo that clearly shows your face.</li>
                <li>Keep one personal account. Don't create accounts for other people, share your account, or open a new account after a suspension.</li>
                <li>Only upload identity documents that belong to you, are valid and haven't been altered.</li>
                <li>Describe yourself, your vehicle and your trips accurately. Don't mislead other members about who will be in the car.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>2. Safety on the road</h2>
            <h3>Drivers</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Hold a valid driver's licence for the class of vehicle you drive and carry the insurance and registration required in your province or territory.</li>
                <li>Keep the vehicle roadworthy and drive within the law, including speed limits and hands-free rules for phones.</li>
                <li>Never drive while impaired by alcohol, cannabis, other drugs, medication or fatigue.</li>
                <li>Have a working seatbelt for every passenger and don't carry more people than there are seatbelts.</li>
                <li>Agree on pickup and drop-off points that are legal and safe to stop at.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Everyone</h3>
            <ul>
                <li>Wear a seatbelt for the whole trip.</li>
                <li>Use child car seats that meet provincial requirements for any child travelling with you.</li>
                <li>Don't use alcohol or cannabis in the vehicle.</li>
                <li>You can end a trip at any safe point if you feel unsafe. No one may pressure you to continue.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>3. Respect and non-discrimination</h2>
            <p>
                Treat every member with courtesy. We don't tolerate discrimination based on race, national or ethnic origin, colour, religion, age, sex,
                sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, marital or family status, disability, or any other ground protected by Canadian human rights law.
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Don't refuse, cancel on, or treat a member differently because of who they are.</li>
                <li>Safety features that DashLane provides — such as women-only rides when they launch — are not discrimination and are allowed.</li>
                <li>Respect the ride preferences that people set, such as quiet rides, music, pets and no smoking.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>4. Harassment and unwanted contact</h2>
            <p>DashLane has <strong>zero tolerance</strong> for:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Threats, intimidation, physical violence or aggressive behaviour.</li>
                <li>Sexual harassment, sexual comments, unwanted touching, or any sexual activity with another member during a trip.</li>
                <li>Hate speech, slurs or symbols that target people for who they are.</li>
                <li>Contacting a member after they've asked you to stop, or using their details for anything other than an arranged trip.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>A single serious incident can result in permanent removal from DashLane.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>5. Reliability and communication</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Be on time for pickups. If you're running late, let the others know as soon as you can.</li>
                <li>If you need to cancel, do it as early as possible; repeated late cancellations or no-shows affect your standing.</li>
                <li>Stick to the agreed route, stops and timing unless everyone agrees to change them.</li>
                <li>Respect luggage limits and the space agreed for each person.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>6. Fair cost-sharing</h2>
            <p>
                DashLane is for sharing trips you're already making, not for running a commercial transport service. Contributions should reasonably reflect the
                costs of the trip, such as fuel and tolls. Drivers are responsible for complying with their province's or territory's rules on carpooling and
                passenger transport. Never ask for extra money, change the agreed amount during a trip, or require payment outside what was agreed.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>7. Privacy of other members</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Use other members' names, numbers and trip details only to arrange and complete the trip.</li>
                <li>Don't share, post or publish another member's personal information, photos or messages.</li>
                <li>Don't record audio or video of other members without the clear consent of everyone in the vehicle, unless the law requires otherwise.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>8. Prohibited items and activities</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Transporting illegal goods, weapons, or anything that requires a permit you don't have.</li>
                <li>Carrying hazardous materials or items that could injure passengers.</li>
                <li>Smoking or vaping in the vehicle unless everyone has agreed and it's legal.</li>
                <li>Using DashLane for any illegal purpose, for fraud or scams, or to recruit members for other services.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>9. Pets and belongings</h2>
            <p>
                Bring pets only on trips where the driver has allowed them, and keep them in a carrier unless agreed otherwise. Service animals are welcome on every
                trip. Look after your own belongings and treat the driver's vehicle with care.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>10. Reporting a concern</h2>
            <p>
                Tell us about anything that breaks these standards, even if it seems minor; patterns matter. Include the member's name, what happened and when.
                We review every report, keep the reporter's identity confidential where we can, and don't tolerate retaliation against anyone who reports in good faith.
                In-app reporting will arrive with the ride feed.
            </p>
            <div class="legal-contact">
                @if (Site.HasSupportEmail)
                {
                    <span>Report a concern: <a href="mailto:@Site.SupportEmail">@Site.SupportEmail</a></span>
                }
                else
                {
                    <span>This DashLane site hasn't published a reporting address yet.</span>
                }
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>11. How we enforce these standards</h2>
            <p>Depending on how serious the issue is and whether it has happened before, we may:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>remind you of the standards or issue a written warning;</li>
                <li>restrict features or require you to re-verify your identity;</li>
                <li>temporarily suspend your account while we investigate;</li>
                <li>permanently remove your account and block new accounts;</li>
                <li>share information with police when the law requires it or someone's safety is at risk.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>If we take action on your account, we'll tell you why where it's safe to do so, and you can ask us to review the decision.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>12. Changes</h2>
            <p>
                We'll update these standards as DashLane grows, and change the date at the top when we do. These standards sit alongside the
                <a class="legal-inline-link" href="@Url.Action("Terms", "Home")">Terms of Service</a> and the
                <a class="legal-inline-link" href="@Url.Action("Privacy", "Home")">Privacy Policy</a>.
            </p>
        </section>

        <nav class="legal-nav" aria-label="Related pages">
            <a class="legal-nav-link" href="@Url.Action("Terms", "Home")">@T("Terms of Service")</a>
            <a class="legal-nav-link" href="@Url.Action("Privacy", "Home")">@T("Privacy Policy")</a>
            <a class="legal-nav-link" href="@Url.Action("Help", "Home")">@T("Help Centre")</a>
            <a class="legal-nav-link" href="@Url.Action("Community", "Home")">@T("Back to getting started")</a>
        </nav>
    </article>
</div>
